{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Mocking.</b> It is an expression of idolatry, an expression of murder, an expression of sexual immorality. For Ishmael and Isaac would quarrel over the inheritance, and Ishmael would say to Isaac, 'I am the firstborn and I take a double portion,' and he would go out to the field and shoot arrows at him. As it is written (Proverbs 26:18–19): ״כמתלהלה היורה זיקים חצים ומות כן איש רמה את רעהו ואמר הלא מצחק אני״. And we learn this from Sarah's reply: ״כי לא יירש בן האמה״ — thus Rashi, of blessed memory, interpreted." "<b>And the sage</b> R. E. interpreted מצחק as playing, in the manner of any lad, and Sarah our mother was jealous of him because he was older than her son." "<b>But</b> the Ramban, of blessed memory, interpreted מצחק as mocking, and because of this she said ״את בן הגר המצרית״ — that is, the son of a maidservant, for she could have said ״ותרא את ישמעאל מצחק״; therefore Sarah said to him: ״גרש האמה״ and so on. For a slave who mocks his master is liable to death, but I do not wish you to kill him, only to drive him and his mother out. And the thing was grievous in Abraham's eyes, as the verse testifies: ״וירע הדבר מאד בעיני אברהם״; and it says ״על אודות בנו״ — this reveals Abraham's merit, that it was not grievous to him on account of attachment to the concubine but only on account of his son, for had she said to drive out the concubine alone, it would not have been hard in his eyes."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:58.738057960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}